ghidra (12.1.4-0lemesre1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Build from source of upstream 12.1.4 for Debian trixie and later,
    amd64 and arm64.
  * Packaging derived from Kali Linux (ghidra 12.1.4+ds-0kali1, Apache-2.0):
    - Gradle pinned to the release of the upstream wrapper (9.7.1) and
      checked by SHA-256 before use;
    - installed in /usr/lib/ghidra, the tree holds architecture-dependent
      native tools;
    - desktop entry and icons, ghidra-analyzeHeadless and
      ghidra-pyghidraRun commands;
    - on arm64, which has no 7-Zip-JBinding library, the built-in zip
      support is enabled for every launcher (launch.properties) instead of
      patching ghidraRun alone;
    - no repack: the orig tarball is the upstream tag archive;
    - build under C.UTF-8: bundled jars hold non-ASCII class names that
      the C locale of a build chroot cannot map to paths;
    - SLEIGH and p-code reference manuals built as PDF (docbook-xsl,
      resolved locally through the XML catalog);
    - executable bit kept on ELF objects and scripts only, no empty
      debug package (native tools are built without -g).
    - GhidraClass training binaries (x86-64 in every package) shipped as
      upstream built them: not stripped, not processed by dh_dwz nor
      dh_shlibdeps.

 -- Eric Lemesre <eric.lemesre@gmail.com>  Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:30:00 +0200
